                <pb facs="0856" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Horn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-02T15:00:00-03:50">July 2, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. Department’s 23, July 1, noon. Minister for Foreign Affairs could not grant
                    me interview until 2 p.m. today. He told me Paraguay considers the incident as
                    closed with the notes of the Chancellery to the Bolivian Legation. He added that
                    the recourse to good offices is entirely disproportionate to the incident which
                    his Government considers as banal.</p>
                <p>Bolivian Minister is still in Asunción.</p>
                <p>Foregoing has been cabled to American Legation at La Paz.</p>
                <p>Text of last Bolivian and Paraguayan notes will be cabled as soon as available
                    which will probably be tomorrow morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
